{"title":"Career Roadmap · 3D Animator","role":"3D Animator","summary":"A 3D Animator creates movement and performance for digitally created characters, creatures, objects, environments and visual effects.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Motion / Animation / VFX Design"},"about":[{"label":"Career","text":"3D Animator"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A 3D Animator creates movement and performance for digitally created characters, creatures, objects, environments and visual effects."},{"type":"h","text":"3D animators work across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Animated films"},{"text":"Feature films"},{"text":"VFX"},{"text":"OTT"},{"text":"Games"},{"text":"Advertising"},{"text":"Product visualisation"},{"text":"Architectural visualisation"},{"text":"Virtual production"},{"text":"Motion design"},{"text":"AR/VR"},{"text":"Digital media"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines animation principles, acting, storytelling, anatomy, cinematography, 3D software and technical problem-solving."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong 3D Animator is not simply someone who can operate Maya or Blender. The core skill is the ability to create convincing movement, weight, timing, emotion and visual storytelling."}]},{"heading":"Typical Education Route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Animation/VFX","3D Animation","Character/Creature Animation","Internship","Junior 3D Animator","3D Animator","Senior Animator","Animation Supervisor","Animation Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative routes include:"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Animation → Games"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Animation → VFX"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Animation → Motion Design"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Animation → Virtual Production"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Animation → Technical Animation"}]},{"heading":"Career Development Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Horizon","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Drawing, animation principles, observation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"3D software, body mechanics, character animation"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Advanced animation, acting, production workflows"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Showreel, industry project, internship"}],[{"text":"0–2 Years"},{"text":"Junior 3D Animator"}],[{"text":"3–6 Years"},{"text":"3D Character/Creature Animator"}],[{"text":"6–10 Years"},{"text":"Senior Animator / Animation Lead"}],[{"text":"10+ Years"},{"text":"Animation Supervisor / Animation Director"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Animation Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first year should focus heavily on traditional animation principles, even if the ultimate goal is 3D."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn the 12 classic animation principles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Squash and stretch"},{"text":"Anticipation"},{"text":"Staging"},{"text":"Straight-ahead and pose-to-pose animation"},{"text":"Follow-through"},{"text":"Slow in/slow out"},{"text":"Arcs"},{"text":"Secondary action"},{"text":"Timing"},{"text":"Exaggeration"},{"text":"Solid drawing"},{"text":"Appeal"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Also develop"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figure drawing"},{"text":"Gesture drawing"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Acting basics"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Cinematography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software introduction"},{"type":"h","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"Maya"},{"text":"Adobe After Effects"},{"text":"Photoshop"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Do not try to master every application simultaneously."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 Portfolio Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Bouncing Ball Animation Study\""},{"type":"p","text":"Create progressively more complex animations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic bouncing ball"},{"text":"Ball with different weights"},{"text":"Ball interacting with an object"},{"text":"Pendulum/overlap study"},{"text":"Character lifting an object"},{"text":"Walk cycle"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This may appear simple, but it establishes the fundamentals of timing, spacing, weight and physics."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — 3D Animation Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Move into professional 3D animation."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D modelling fundamentals"},{"text":"Rigging fundamentals"},{"text":"Character setup"},{"text":"Keyframe animation"},{"text":"Graph editor"},{"text":"Body mechanics"},{"text":"Walk cycles"},{"text":"Run cycles"},{"text":"Jumps"},{"text":"Weight shifts"},{"text":"Facial animation"},{"text":"Camera animation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software"},{"type":"h","text":"Prioritise one primary 3D package:"},{"type":"h","text":"Maya or Blender"},{"type":"h","text":"Then develop supporting skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Substance 3D"},{"text":"ZBrush"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"After Effects"},{"text":"Premiere Pro"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 Portfolio Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Character Body Mechanics Reel\""},{"type":"h","text":"Create 5–6 short shots:"},{"type":"h","text":"Shot 1"},{"type":"h","text":"Character lifting a heavy object"},{"type":"h","text":"Shot 2"},{"type":"h","text":"Character jumping"},{"type":"h","text":"Shot 3"},{"type":"h","text":"Character running"},{"type":"h","text":"Shot 4"},{"type":"h","text":"Character pushing/pulling something"},{"type":"h","text":"Shot 5"},{"type":"h","text":"Character falling"},{"type":"h","text":"Shot 6"},{"type":"h","text":"Character interacting with another character"},{"type":"p","text":"Each shot should demonstrate a different animation challenge."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Character Animation"},{"type":"p","text":"Year 3 should move toward performance and acting."},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Character acting"},{"text":"Facial animation"},{"text":"Lip synchronisation"},{"text":"Emotion"},{"text":"Body language"},{"text":"Dialogue animation"},{"text":"Creature animation"},{"text":"Advanced body mechanics"},{"text":"Camera language"},{"text":"Cinematic staging"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Acting exercises"},{"type":"h","text":"Animate characters who:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"React to unexpected information"},{"text":"Are angry"},{"text":"Are frightened"},{"text":"Are excited"},{"text":"Are confused"},{"text":"Try to hide something"},{"text":"Interact with another character"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The goal is to communicate emotion without relying entirely on dialogue."}]},{"heading":"Advanced Specialisations","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Character Animator"},{"text":"Human/character performance"}],[{"text":"Creature Animator"},{"text":"Animals and fictional creatures"}],[{"text":"Facial Animator"},{"text":"Facial performance"}],[{"text":"Cinematic Animator"},{"text":"Film/game cinematics"}],[{"text":"Game Animator"},{"text":"Real-time character animation"}],[{"text":"VFX Animator"},{"text":"Animation within visual-effects production"}],[{"text":"Motion Designer"},{"text":"Motion graphics and visual communication"}],[{"text":"Technical Animator"},{"text":"Rigging, tools and animation systems"}],[{"text":"Crowd Animator"},{"text":"Large-scale character movement"}],[{"text":"Previsualisation Artist"},{"text":"Pre-production visualisation"}],[{"text":"Virtual Production Animator"},{"text":"Real-time 3D environments"}],[{"text":"Medical Animator"},{"text":"Scientific/medical visualisation"}],[{"text":"Product Animator"},{"text":"Product/brand animation"}],[{"text":"Architectural Animator"},{"text":"Architectural visualisation"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 3 Technical Development","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of the complete production pipeline."},{"type":"h","text":"Pipeline"},{"type":"h","text":"Concept"},{"type":"h","text":"Modelling"},{"type":"h","text":"Texturing"},{"type":"h","text":"Rigging"},{"type":"h","text":"Animation"},{"type":"h","text":"Lighting"},{"type":"h","text":"Rendering"},{"type":"h","text":"Compositing"},{"type":"h","text":"Editing"},{"type":"p","text":"A 3D Animator does not necessarily need to master every department, but understanding the entire pipeline makes collaboration much easier."}]},{"heading":"Year 4 — Industry Readiness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The final year should focus heavily on creating a professional animation showreel."},{"type":"h","text":"Graduation Project"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Cinematic Character Sequence\""},{"type":"p","text":"Create a 60–120 second sequence with a clear story."},{"type":"h","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"A robot discovers an abandoned city and encounters a mysterious object."},{"type":"h","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Character design"},{"text":"Environment"},{"text":"Storyboard"},{"text":"Layout"},{"text":"Camera planning"},{"text":"Character acting"},{"text":"Body mechanics"},{"text":"Facial performance"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Rendering"},{"text":"Compositing"},{"text":"Sound"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The animation should demonstrate performance rather than simply technical movement."}]},{"heading":"Internship Targets","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Look for internships at:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Animation studios"},{"text":"VFX studios"},{"text":"Game studios"},{"text":"Film-production companies"},{"text":"Advertising agencies"},{"text":"Motion-design studios"},{"text":"OTT production houses"},{"text":"Virtual production companies"},{"text":"Architectural visualisation studios"},{"text":"Animation outsourcing studios"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship roles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D Animation Intern"},{"text":"Character Animation Intern"},{"text":"VFX Animation Intern"},{"text":"Game Animation Intern"},{"text":"Motion Design Intern"},{"text":"Previsualisation Intern"},{"text":"Technical Animation Intern"},{"text":"3D Generalist Intern"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"\"60-Second Character Performance\""},{"type":"p","text":"Create a short cinematic animation around one character."},{"type":"h","text":"Requirements"},{"type":"h","text":"Story"},{"type":"p","text":"A simple but emotionally understandable narrative."},{"type":"h","text":"Animation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Walk"},{"text":"Run"},{"text":"Interaction"},{"text":"Body mechanics"},{"text":"Facial acting"},{"text":"Dialogue/non-verbal acting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rig"},{"text":"Camera"},{"text":"Lighting"},{"text":"Rendering"},{"text":"Compositing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Full animation"},{"text":"Breakdown"},{"text":"Animation reel extract"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This is much more valuable for an animator's portfolio than a collection of unrelated 3D renders."}]},{"heading":"Animation Software Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Primary"},{"type":"h","text":"Choose one:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maya"},{"text":"Blender"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Sculpting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ZBrush"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Texturing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Substance 3D Painter"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rendering"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn one or more:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arnold"},{"text":"V-Ray"},{"text":"Redshift"},{"text":"Blender Cycles"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Compositing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Nuke"},{"text":"After Effects"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Editing"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Premiere Pro"},{"text":"DaVinci Resolve"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Real-time"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Unity"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal stack depends on whether the student targets film/VFX, animation, games or motion design."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Useful learning areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D animation"},{"text":"Character animation"},{"text":"Acting for animation"},{"text":"Rigging fundamentals"},{"text":"VFX"},{"text":"Cinematography"},{"text":"Storyboarding"},{"text":"Motion design"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Game animation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For animation careers, showreel quality is substantially more important than collecting certificates."}]},{"heading":"Jobs After Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Potential roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Junior 3D Animator"},{"text":"3D Character Animator"},{"text":"VFX Animator"},{"text":"Game Animator"},{"text":"Creature Animator"},{"text":"Motion Designer"},{"text":"Cinematic Animator"},{"text":"3D Generalist"},{"text":"Previsualisation Artist"},{"text":"Technical Animator"},{"text":"Animation Artist"},{"text":"Virtual Production Artist"}]}]},{"heading":"Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Animation questions"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What are the 12 principles of animation?"},{"text":"What is the difference between timing and spacing?"},{"text":"How do you communicate weight?"},{"text":"How do you make a character feel alive?"},{"text":"Explain your animation workflow."},{"text":"How do you approach a dialogue shot?"},{"text":"How do you animate a heavy versus light object?"},{"text":"What is anticipation?"},{"text":"What is follow-through?"},{"text":"How do you improve a weak animation?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical test"},{"type":"h","text":"You may be asked to animate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"A walk cycle"},{"text":"A jump"},{"text":"A character picking up an object"},{"text":"A short acting shot"},{"text":"A dialogue sequence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"The evaluator will usually look at:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Timing","spacing","weight","posing","arcs","acting","polish."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Possible directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Animation"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced character and production skills."},{"type":"h","text":"VFX"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Film"},{"text":"Television"},{"text":"OTT"},{"text":"CGI"},{"text":"Creature work"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Game animation"},{"text":"Real-time animation"},{"text":"Cinematics"},{"text":"Interactive storytelling"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Motion Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Advertising"},{"text":"Branding"},{"text":"Digital media"},{"text":"Broadcast"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Virtual Production"},{"type":"h","text":"Useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Real-time filmmaking"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Virtual sets"},{"text":"Previsualisation"}]}]},{"heading":"High-Value Specialist Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Film Character Animator"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Maya/Blender","Character Animation","Acting","Film/VFX","Character Animator"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — Game Animator"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Animation","Unreal/Unity","Game Animation","Gameplay/Cinematics"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Creature Animator"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Anatomy","Animal Motion","Creature Animation","VFX"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — Technical Animator"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Animation","Rigging","Python/Scripting","Technical Animation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route E — Virtual Production"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","3D","Unreal Engine","Real-time Animation","Virtual Production"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route F — Medical Animation"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","3D","Anatomy","Scientific Visualisation","Medical Animator"]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio / Showreel Requirements","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For an animator, the showreel is the primary career asset."},{"type":"h","text":"Target:"},{"type":"h","text":"60–90 second main reel"},{"type":"p","text":"Include your strongest work first."},{"type":"h","text":"Possible shots:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Character acting"},{"text":"Dialogue"},{"text":"Body mechanics"},{"text":"Walk/run"},{"text":"Creature movement"},{"text":"Interaction"},{"text":"Cinematic shot"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also maintain individual project breakdowns."},{"type":"h","text":"Do not fill the reel with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Weak exercises"},{"text":"Repetitive walk cycles"},{"text":"Unfinished shots"},{"text":"Generic AI-generated animation"},{"text":"Work you cannot explain"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Quality > quantity."}]},{"heading":"Professional Animation Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Brief"},{"type":"h","text":"Story / Script"},{"type":"h","text":"Storyboard"},{"type":"h","text":"Animatic"},{"type":"h","text":"Layout"},{"type":"h","text":"Blocking"},{"type":"h","text":"Spline"},{"type":"h","text":"Polish"},{"type":"h","text":"Facial/Secondary Animation"},{"type":"h","text":"Lighting"},{"type":"h","text":"Rendering"},{"type":"h","text":"Compositing"},{"type":"h","text":"Editing"},{"type":"h","text":"Final Delivery"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding this workflow prepares students for studio production."}]},{"heading":"AI in 3D Animation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI is rapidly changing animation workflows."},{"type":"h","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion capture cleanup"},{"text":"Pose generation"},{"text":"Facial animation"},{"text":"Lip synchronisation"},{"text":"Rotoscoping"},{"text":"Background generation"},{"text":"Concept development"},{"text":"Procedural animation"},{"text":"Animation reference"},{"text":"Motion synthesis"},{"text":"Rendering assistance"},{"text":"Video generation"},{"text":"Asset creation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI-generated motion does not automatically have good:"},{"type":"flow","items":["acting","timing","storytelling","weight","intentional posing."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The animator's role increasingly shifts toward creative direction, performance, editing and refinement, while automation handles portions of repetitive production work."}]},{"heading":"Future of 3D Animation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Major growth areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Real-time animation"},{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Virtual production"},{"text":"AI-assisted animation"},{"text":"Motion capture"},{"text":"Performance capture"},{"text":"Procedural animation"},{"text":"Interactive storytelling"},{"text":"Games"},{"text":"AR/VR"},{"text":"Digital humans"},{"text":"Virtual characters"},{"text":"Real-time cinematics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest future profile will combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Animation","storytelling","real-time 3D","AI-assisted workflows."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Career Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"The profession is likely to evolve from:"},{"type":"h","text":"Traditional keyframe animation"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Digital 3D animation"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Motion/performance capture"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Real-time animation"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Procedural animation"},{"type":"h","text":"→ AI-assisted animation"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Interactive characters"},{"type":"h","text":"→ Adaptive digital performers"},{"type":"p","text":"This does not eliminate the need for animators. It changes the value of the animator toward performance direction, creative decision-making and high-level animation control."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad Opportunities","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students can explore animation and VFX ecosystems in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"United States"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"United Kingdom"},{"text":"France"},{"text":"Japan"},{"text":"South Korea"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"New Zealand"},{"text":"Germany"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Relevant postgraduate areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D Animation"},{"text":"Character Animation"},{"text":"VFX"},{"text":"Game Animation"},{"text":"Computer Animation"},{"text":"Motion Design"},{"text":"Virtual Production"},{"text":"Digital Arts"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong showreel is usually more important than academic marks alone for specialised animation programmes."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior 3D Animator"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Animation fundamentals"},{"text":"Production shots"},{"text":"Technical workflow"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3–5 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Character/Creature Animator"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Complex shots"},{"text":"Acting"},{"text":"Cinematics"},{"text":"Performance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Animator"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"High-difficulty shots"},{"text":"Mentoring"},{"text":"Quality control"}]},{"type":"h","text":"8–12 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Animation Lead / Animation Supervisor"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Team leadership"},{"text":"Shot reviews"},{"text":"Production planning"},{"text":"Creative direction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"12+ Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Animation Director / Creative Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Overall animation style"},{"text":"Character performance"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Production leadership"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Animation"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"12 principles"},{"text":"Timing"},{"text":"Spacing"},{"text":"Posing"},{"text":"Weight"},{"text":"Body mechanics"},{"text":"Acting"},{"text":"Facial animation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"3D"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Maya or Blender"},{"text":"Rigging fundamentals"},{"text":"3D workflow"},{"text":"Rendering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Supporting"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"ZBrush"},{"text":"Substance 3D"},{"text":"Nuke/After Effects"},{"text":"Premiere/Resolve"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Real-Time"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Unreal Engine"},{"text":"Real-time animation"},{"text":"Virtual production"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Creative"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Cinematography"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Editing"},{"text":"Character development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Motion capture"},{"text":"AI-assisted animation"},{"text":"Procedural animation"},{"text":"Digital humans"},{"text":"Interactive characters"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"flow","items":["Drawing","animation principles","observation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"flow","items":["3D software","body mechanics","character animation"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3"},{"type":"flow","items":["Acting","facial animation","advanced production"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4"},{"type":"flow","items":["Major animated short","internship","professional showreel"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Graduation"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior 3D Animator"},{"type":"h","text":"3–6 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"3D Character/Creature Animator"},{"type":"h","text":"6–10 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Animator / Animation Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"10+ Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Animation Supervisor / Animation Director"},{"type":"h","text":"Best Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A highly competitive B.Des 3D Animator graduate should demonstrate:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Excellent animation fundamentals","strong Maya/Blender proficiency","body mechanics","character acting","facial animation","storytelling","cinematography","production-pipeline awareness","Unreal Engine familiarity","5–8 exceptional animation shots","industry internship","a polished 60–90 second showreel."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The biggest differentiator is not the number of software packages known. It is the quality of the animator's timing, posing, weight, acting and storytelling. A student with one excellent character-performance shot can be more employable than one with dozens of technically complex but weak animations."}]}]}